# {{ name }}: agent guide

- Repo card: Cortex `entities/{{ name }}` (create it with the service); map: this file until a `docs/` map exists.
- Code rules for every agent: Cortex `docs/skills/repo-hygiene` (read it; it is not copied here).
- Coding standards (read before changing code): [CODING_STANDARDS.md](CODING_STANDARDS.md).
- Platform and library: [homelab-common](https://github.com/navaneethkrishna30/homelab-common) `SPEC.md`.
- Branches: `main` released and tagged, `dev` integration, work branches from `dev`.
- Domain terms: [GLOSSARY.md](GLOSSARY.md); use its words in code, tickets and commits. Platform terms (service,
  gateway, schema, actor, audit, ...) are defined in homelab-common's [GLOSSARY.md](https://github.com/navaneethkrishna30/homelab-common/blob/main/GLOSSARY.md), not here.
- Decisions already made: [docs/adr/](docs/adr/); read the ones touching your area, flag any you contradict.

## Layout
`src/{{ package }}/`: `app.py` (create_app), `settings.py`, `models.py` (tables and API payloads), `api.py` (REST),
`tools.py` (MCP tools, also plain functions). `migrations/` Alembic, forward only; `config/config.yaml` tunables.

## Commands
`just` is not installed; run it as `uvx --from rust-just just <recipe>`.
- `check`: sync, lint, types, test, validate (service.yaml), secrets-guard
- New migration: `uv run alembic revision --autogenerate -m "<what>"` (needs a database), review it, commit it.

## Agent skills

### Issue tracker

Vikunja (service `tasks`), project `{{ name }}`; commits and PR bodies end with `Task: tasks#<id>`. See
`docs/agents/issue-tracker.md`.

### Triage labels

The five default roles (`needs-triage`, `needs-info`, `ready-for-agent`, `ready-for-human`, `wontfix`) as Vikunja
labels. See `docs/agents/triage-labels.md`.

### Domain docs

Single-context: `GLOSSARY.md` (in place of `CONTEXT.md`) and `docs/adr/`. See `docs/agents/domain.md`.
